    <!-- App Info Screen -->
    <string name="app_info_title">App Information</string>
    <string name="info_expand">Expand</string>
    <string name="info_collapse">Collapse</string>
    
    <string name="info_important_title">IMPORTANT</string>
    <string name="info_important_content">Welcome once again to my application.\n\nThis is a completely free product that I, a student and car enthusiast, initially created only for personal use, but decided to share with you as well. I have no goal to make money from this or gain popularity — I just wanted to build a car logbook that is convenient by my own standards.\n\nAll data is stored only on your device — the app has no server of its own. To avoid losing your records when reinstalling the app or switching phones, there are two backup options (the section with the floppy-disk icon in the main menu):\n\n1) Local export/import. \"Export data\" saves a single archive file (database + all photos and documents) to a location of your choice. Later you can \"import\" this file and your data will be fully restored.\n\n2) Cloud backup to Yandex.Disk. Connect your Yandex account with the button in the same section (a browser opens; the app only gets access to its own CarLog folder on the Disk). After that you can create backups manually, and with auto-backup enabled a copy is created automatically a few minutes after your data changes (when online). The three most recent copies are kept, and you can restore from any of them.\n\nYou can contact me through the contacts listed in the app settings — please report any bugs you find and I will try to fix them in updates.</string>
    
    <string name="info_cars_title">Cars</string>
    <string name="info_cars_content">Here you manage your cars. You can:\n\n• Add new cars with photos and detailed information (make, model, VIN, license plate, fuel type, gas equipment, etc.)\n• Edit car information\n• Delete cars (all related records will also be deleted)\n\nThe car card is the entry point to every section: parts, maintenance, accidents, consumables, refuelings, other expenses, documents and statistics.\n\nThe current mileage is maintained automatically — it always equals the maximum mileage across all records. You can update it manually with the update-mileage button on the card. If you enter a value below the current one, the app warns you and asks for confirmation: once confirmed, records with a higher mileage are lowered to the new value as well — otherwise the previous maximum would come back automatically.</string>
    
    <string name="info_consumables_title">Consumables</string>
    <string name="info_consumables_content">Section for tracking consumable materials:\n\n• 11 standard categories are always visible: engine oil, transmission oil/fluid, brake and coolant fluids, filters (oil, air, fuel, cabin), front and rear brake pads, battery\n• About 30 more optional categories (spark plugs, belts, discs, tires, wiper blades, bulbs, etc.) can be enabled in the section settings\n• For each consumable you specify installation date, mileage, manufacturer, part number, cost (volume for fluids)\n• Replacement intervals by mileage and/or time; custom values can be set in the section settings\n• Traffic-light status on the card: green — all good, yellow — more than half of the resource used, red — replacement is due very soon or overdue\n• Replacement history for each category\n\nThe best way to replace a consumable is via its details screen (the \"Replace\" button) or via scheduled maintenance — the old consumable is archived automatically.\n\nDirect adding also works: if the category already has an active consumable, it is archived as replaced.</string>
    
    <string name="info_parts_title">Parts</string>
    <string name="info_parts_content">Accounting for all parts and assemblies of the car:\n\n• Adding parts with indication of name, manufacturer, part number\n• Installation date and current mileage\n• Cost of the part and installation work\n• Mark about breakdown with indication of date and mileage\n• Ability to replace the part (creates a new record, the old one is marked as broken)\n• Part photos\n• Notes and comments\n\nThis allows you to keep a complete history of all installed parts and track their reliability.</string>
    
    <string name="info_breakdowns_title">Breakdowns</string>
    <string name="info_breakdowns_content">A single log of all work done on the car. Each record has one of three types:\n\n• Repair — fixing a breakdown (can be marked as warranty repair)\n• Scheduled maintenance — requires at least one replaced consumable; old consumables of the same categories are archived automatically\n• Modification — upgrades and improvements\n\nA record includes name, description, date and mileage, parts cost (as a total amount or as a list of specific parts — they will appear in the Parts section), service work cost, service name and address, photos and notes.\n\nHelps track all work on the car and plan the maintenance budget.</string>
    
    <string name="info_accidents_title">Accidents</string>
    <string name="info_accidents_content">Accounting for road traffic accidents:\n\n• Date, mileage and place of the accident\n• Damage description and severity (minor / medium / serious / total)\n• Your role: at fault or victim (the at-fault party can only receive a KASKO payout)\n• Insurance payouts: OSAGO, KASKO, from the culprit\n• Repair cost — as a total amount or as a list of parts (they will appear in the Parts section marked \"Accident\")\n• Photos from the scene and one PDF document (e.g. the accident report) — it can be opened from the details screen\n\nAccident expenses appear in statistics as a separate category that can be excluded from calculations.</string>
    
    <string name="info_refueling_title">Refueling</string>
    <string name="info_refueling_content">Accounting for all car refuelings:\n\n• Date, mileage and refueling location\n• Fuel volume and type (gasoline grades, diesel, gas with LPG/CNG equipment; charges in kWh for electric cars)\n• Cost per liter or total cost (the other one is calculated automatically)\n• \"Full tank\" mark\n\nFuel consumption is calculated automatically between two full-tank refuelings: the full tank\'s liters plus all partial refuelings between them are divided by the distance driven. Partial refuelings therefore have no consumption of their own — mark full tanks to see your consumption.\n\nThe refueling list shows a summary: count, volume, total cost and average consumption.</string>
    
    <string name="info_expenses_title">Other Expenses</string>
    <string name="info_expenses_content">Accounting for all other car expenses:\n\n• Categories: self car wash, accessories, car audio, interior detailing, wheels, tires, other\n• Date, mileage, name and amount of the expense\n• Service information (name, address)\n• Notes\n\nInsurance, technical inspection and vehicle tax are tracked separately — in the Documents section.\n\nAllows you to keep a complete record of all car expenses and analyze their structure.</string>
    
    <string name="info_documents_title">Documents</string>
    <string name="info_documents_content">Keep track of your car documents\' validity:\n\n• Standard types: OSAGO, KASKO, vehicle tax — their tiles are always visible; plus any custom documents via the \"Other\" type\n• For policies the type and expiry date are required; optional: number, insurer, start date, cost, photo, notes\n• For the tax you enter the last assessment date (usually the car registration date) — the app will remind you of the next assessment a year later; the tax has no number or organization fields\n• Traffic-light status: green — more than 30 days left, yellow — 30 days or less, red — 7 days or less or expired\n• The \"Renew\" button archives the old document and creates a new one — the History tab shows how the policy price changes year over year\n• There is always exactly one active document of each standard type\n\nDocument costs appear in statistics as a separate \"Insurance and taxes\" category.</string>

    <string name="info_statistics_title">Statistics</string>
    <string name="info_statistics_content">Detailed car statistics — five tabs:\n\n• General: expense distribution by category, spending trend, cost per km, average km per day and month, the most expensive month\n• Fuel: average consumption, volumes and costs by fuel type, charts\n• Repairs: amounts and counts, parts vs labor breakdown, distribution by work type\n• Other expenses: structure by category, top 5\n• Consumables: average maintenance cost, expenses by category\n\nFilters apply to every tab: period (or a specific month), mileage range, exclude accidents. All data is presented with graphs and charts.</string>
    
